            {
              "value": "Level",
              "text": "Level",
              "hint": "What does it read against what is actually in the vessel? Vessel and technology if you know them, and what the surface does: foam, agitation, coating, a light product.",
              "key": null
            },
            {
              "value": "Flow",
              "text": "Flow",
              "hint": "What does it read against what you expect? Meter type and line size if you know them, and whether the line ever runs partly full, flashes, or carries gas.",
              "key": null
            },
            {
              "value": "Pressure",
              "text": "Pressure",
              "hint": "What does it read against what you expect? Whether it is gauge, differential, or absolute, and what the taps and impulse lines look like.",
              "key": null
            },
            {
              "value": "Temperature",
              "text": "Temperature",
              "hint": "What does it read against a reference? Thermowell or direct, immersion depth if you know it, and how fast the process really moves.",
              "key": null
            },
            {
              "value": "Analytical (pH, conductivity, analyzer)",
              "text": "Analytical (pH, conductivity, analyzer)",
              "hint": "What does it read against a lab or grab sample? How often it is cleaned and calibrated, and what the process does to the sensor between cleanings.",
